From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 07:03:21 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] [build] Build warning-clean with GCC and Clang.

Builds of the whole tree with GCC 15 and Clang 21 for armv7, aarch64 and
x86-64 against Qt 5.15 warned in our own code, and Clang could not build
the telepathy plugin at all:

- Add the missing override to the handler and manager classes. Some of
  their members were already marked, so Clang warned for every other one
  (-Winconsistent-missing-override).
- Drop two unused Q_D in the D-Bus service, and rename locals that shadow
  others (-Wshadow). The telepathy provider's ready() lambda also gets
  the provider as context object, so it can't run after the provider is
  gone.
- TelepathyQt 0.9.8's shared-ptr.h uses the 'register' storage class,
  which C++17 removed. Clang rejects it, and compilers now default to
  C++17, so build the telepathy plugin as C++14.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
